.TH "SIDE-DOG-TMUX" "1" "September 8, 2026" "Side Dog" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
\&side\-dog\-tmux \- coding\-agent activity viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS AND OPTIONS
.nf
\&side\-dog tmux [options]
\&
\&
\&\-h, \-\-help
\&  show this help message and exit
\&
\&project ([PROJECT])
\&
\&
\&\-\-width WIDTH
\&
.fi
.SH FIRST RUN
.nf
\&side\-dog \-\-version
\&side\-dog demo \-\-watch
\&side\-dog doctor .
\&side\-dog watch .
.fi
.SH VIEWS
Watch is chronological. Press b for Board contributions, a for its live
roster, and w to return.
Board --activity groups recorded work by repository, issue/PR, session and
event-time model over the last 24 hours.
Use j/k to select work and o to open its link. Completed contributors remain
in recorded history.
Unknown attribution is explicit. GitHub polling is an observation, never model
effort.
Only unambiguous recorded turn references link work; ambiguous actions remain
unlinked.
.SH FILES
~/.config/side-dog/config.toml: hand-authored configuration.
.br
~/.config/side-dog/spaces.toml: saved spaces, rewritten by watch --save.
.br
~/.local/state/side-dog/: disposable validated activity and display state.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
XDG_CONFIG_HOME overrides the configuration parent. SIDE_DOG_STATE_DIR
overrides runtime state.
.SH PRIVACY
Only validated metadata is persisted or exposed; never prompts, responses,
full commands, output, diffs or file contents.
Usage estimates are not allocated to PRs.
.SH SEE ALSO
side-dog(1), side-dog-watch(1), side-dog-board(1), side-dog-doctor(1)
.br
https://qfennessy.github.io/side-dog/
